	<p class="…">{{> "dateline"}}</p>

Only the text, because the wrapper's type size, colour and spacing are part of the drawing of
the card around it and differ on every one of them. What is shared is the two values and their
separator, and those are exactly what is easy to get wrong twice: the date format, and
`reading_time`'s three translated forms.

`reading_time` is computed by Ghost from word count and image count and stored nowhere, so the
label is whatever the body length implies — never a field a fixture can set. --}}
